From 7eb959fcc9299ffb6b32f8339e7c3cc634b0ebdb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 14:59:55 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 905/906] media: i2c: Add Sony IMX596 and GalaxyCore GC02M1
 sensor drivers

Front (IMX596, 20 MP, 4-lane D-PHY) and macro (GC02M1, 2 MP, 1-lane
D-PHY) cameras of the Xiaomi 12T Pro (diting). As the s5k4h7 driver,
both load their initialisation and mode register tables from a
"camregs" firmware built from the camera module data (CAMREGS1 or
CAMREGS2 with bursts). The modes, link frequencies, pixel rates, chip
IDs and power-up orders come from the module data.

IMX596: CCS-style registers (0x0202 exposure, 0x0204 analogue gain,
0x0340 frame length), modes 5184x3904, 2592x1952, 2592x1458, 1280x720.
GC02M1: 8-bit register addresses in pages (0xfe), exposure 0x03/0x04,
frame length 0x41/0x42, global pre-gain 0xb1/0xb2, stream 0x3e.
The Bayer order is selectable with the "bayer" module parameter for
the bring-up.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
